    "body": "## Problem\n\nAn out-of-range number in 'iskeyword', 'isfname' or 'isident' crashes Nvim, e.g. from a modeline (#42409):\n\n```\n# vim: iskeyword=1-100000000000000000000000:\n```\n\n`parse_isopt()` reads the numbers with `getdigits_int(..., strict=true, ...)`, which calls `abort()` on `intmax_t` overflow and hits an `assert` for values outside `int` range (`iskeyword=4294967361`). In a release build that second value would be truncated to an `int` instead.\n\n## Solution\n\nParse the numbers non-strictly. An out-of-range value becomes 0, which the existing range check already rejects with E474.\n\nTests: added both values to the invalid-value table in `test/functional/api/vim_spec.lua`. Without the fix the test fails (Nvim exits with SIGABRT, status 134); with the fix it passes. Checked by hand with the modeline from the issue: it now reports `E474: Invalid argument` and leaves 'iskeyword' unchanged.\n\nFixes #42409\n\nAI-assisted: I reviewed the change and ran the tests above.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-16T23:33:12Z",
